{"body":{"asks":"Whether a holon that already exists arrives in a store when a whole kept there comes to hold it, with what it holds in turn, and leaves a store when no whole there holds it any longer, so every store stays whole if taken away; or whether a whole may hold, across stores, what another store keeps. Today a holon stays where it is kept, so the engine cannot move one: the twenty-second session cut the components out of glass into a store of their own by one act written to each strata store, every id kept, unjudged by the engine.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M75GVPQVR6903M"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M75GVW5PG86000","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Residence follows holding"}
{"body":{"asks":"How the engine, the language, the interface and a store's own code know a store's root: today by its type's name, store, in four places, so a type of that name anywhere would make roots; and the store contract gives no way to ask which holon is the root, so the location finds it as the holon nothing else holds. One home for that fact, perhaps glass's own type by reference, or the foundational types, store, shape and dependency, named in the store contract, as the twenty-second session proposed.","raised":[{"$ref":"1M75J2R7D9MQ03R"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M75J2S6MNFN000","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"How a root is known"}
{"body":{"asks":"Left for the author to weigh after the twenty-second session took the code's binding to components, the address's hidden step and the chassis's link file away: what a card says, written in the language as one function; whether asking, the bar shown or not, a class on the page's body found by selectors, and a list's chosen look are state in the field, buffers, rather than the browser's; a card a component of its own; the holon as the native holon gives it, decoded in one place; and the chassis kept apart from its renderer, each concern a file of its own.","raised":[{"$ref":"1M84FFJ1DN05000"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M84FFJ1DN05001","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"The components' remaining glue"}
{"body":{"asks":"How a store is let go: the store contract gives read, offer and subscribe, and nothing tells a store it is no longer wanted, so strata keeps its files and timers once unmounted. The location listens to the browser only from its first subscriber to its last, so an engine unmounting it lets it go; most stores are not so shaped. A clear task for the near future, at the author's word.","raised":[{"$ref":"1M87MM071Z6P000"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M87MM071Z6P003","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Stopping a store"}
{"body":{"asks":"Whether addresses and dependencies resolve through a store's identity, its root's id, rather than the name it was mounted under: a reference by id names no store and survives stores moving, while an address begins at a mount's local name, and a dependency names the store it stands on by name alone; for the long run, not the pilot.","raised":[{"$ref":"1M87MM071Z6P001"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M87MM071Z6P004","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Addresses through a store's identity"}
{"body":{"asks":"How a running integration finds the .glass it ships: on a machine beside its code, in a page where the site publishes stores, a URL bound to the site's layout, which cannot stay; to be taken up with the git integration.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M87MM071Z6P002"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M87MM071Z6P005","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Where an integration finds its own store"}